Cell["\<\
I wanted to be able to make a fractal of any word, so I needed to adapt the \
code. First, I defined the function R(x) for the transformation matrix of x \
degrees counterclockwise rotation and then wrote out all of the \
transformations for letters A-Z in alphabetical order in the form:
{list of scale factors for horizontal stretch (all vertical scaling is just \
1/6) for each vertex, list of R(degrees of counterclockwise rotation) for \
each vertex, list of translation matrices for each vertex}\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9810992215929403`*^9, 3.981099284500271*^9}, {
  3.98110695393071*^9, 3.981106977623629*^9}, {3.9811091655114183`*^9, 
  3.9811094509401007`*^9}, {3.981110026119767*^9, 
  3.9811100435727663`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"51223c0a-b17f-47bd-badf-\
6eb5dfcb84ba"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

